Run a rotating HydraCam master/slave capture matrix. Each capture-capable
device is launched once as master. Every other discovered target is launched
as a forced slave pointed at that master's Wi-Fi host, then the capture
scenario is sent only through the master automation bridge.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --ios-host DEVICE_ID=HOST
                        Explicit bridge host for a physical iOS device. May
                        repeat.
  --auto-ios-bridge-hosts, --no-auto-ios-bridge-hosts
                        Scan likely LAN hosts for physical iOS automation
                        bridges and adopt only identity-matched /healthz
                        responses. Enabled by the immediate role-switch
                        shortcuts unless --no-auto-ios-bridge-hosts is passed.
  --ios-bridge-scan-subnet CIDR
                        Extra IPv4 subnet to scan for identity-matched
                        physical iOS bridges when --auto-ios-bridge-hosts is
                        enabled. May repeat.
  --run-dir RUN_DIR
  --dry-run
  --warm-summary WARM_SUMMARY
                        Reuse targets and masterHosts from a previous
                        rotating-matrix summary.json or run directory,
                        skipping flutter/adb discovery and master-host
                        probing.
  --use-latest-warm-summary, --no-use-latest-warm-summary
                        Reuse the latest persisted warm bridge map instead of
                        running Flutter/ADB discovery. Immediate role-switch
                        shortcuts use this cache automatically when it exists;
                        pass --no-use-latest-warm-summary to force fresh
                        discovery.
  --latest-warm-summary LATEST_WARM_SUMMARY
                        Path to the persisted latest warm bridge map used by
                        --use-latest-warm-summary and updated after successful
                        warm role-switch runs.
  --update-latest-warm-summary, --no-update-latest-warm-summary
                        Update the latest warm bridge map after a successful
                        warm role-switch run. Disable with --no-update-latest-
                        warm-summary.
  --target-id TARGET_ID
                        Only include this device ID in the run. May repeat.
                        Filtering happens before physical iOS host validation.
  --expect-target-id EXPECT_TARGET_ID
                        Require this device ID to be present after
                        discovery/warm-summary loading and target filtering.
                        May repeat. The runner fails before
                        build/install/launch when an expected target is
                        absent.
  --master-id MASTER_ID
                        Only run rotations where this device ID is master. May
                        repeat.
  --skip-build
  --skip-install
  --apk APK
  --android-ndk-version ANDROID_NDK_VERSION
                        Override the Gradle hydracamNdkVersion property for
                        this build. Useful when the default repo NDK is not
                        installed locally.
  --android-port-base ANDROID_PORT_BASE
  --local-port-base LOCAL_PORT_BASE
  --physical-ios-port PHYSICAL_IOS_PORT
  --record-seconds RECORD_SECONDS
  --timeout TIMEOUT
  --standby-launch-timeout STANDBY_LAUNCH_TIMEOUT
                        Maximum seconds to wait for initial standby bridges in
                        runtime role-switch mode. Defaults to --timeout.
  --role-switch-verify-timeout ROLE_SWITCH_VERIFY_TIMEOUT
                        Maximum seconds to wait after a warm runtime role
                        switch for the promoted master commands and expected
                        client connections.
  --capture-stage-timeout CAPTURE_STAGE_TIMEOUT
                        Maximum seconds to wait for start-session/photo/end-
                        session state on all targets in a rotation.
  --recording-ready-timeout RECORDING_READY_TIMEOUT
                        Maximum seconds to wait for all required targets to
                        report isRecording before the runner starts the
                        record-seconds timer.
  --stop-recording-timeout STOP_RECORDING_TIMEOUT
                        Maximum seconds to wait for all required targets to
                        save a video after stop_recording.
  --macos-master-host MACOS_MASTER_HOST
                        Explicit Wi-Fi/LAN IP other devices should use when
                        macOS is master.
  --fast-ios-launch     Use preinstalled physical iOS apps launched through
                        devicectl runtime environment instead of flutter run.
  --ios-profile-build-install
                        Build and install an automation-enabled iOS Profile
                        app on selected physical iOS devices before launch.
                        Use this once to make --fast-ios-launch viable without
                        Flutter tooling.
  --ios-profile-app IOS_PROFILE_APP
                        Path to the built iOS Profile Runner.app to install.
  --xctrace-ios-launch  Use xctrace to launch preinstalled physical iOS apps.
                        This is useful for older devices that appear in
                        xcdevice but not devicectl.
  --xctrace-time-limit-seconds XCTRACE_TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS
                        How long xctrace should keep a launched physical iOS
                        app alive. Only used with --xctrace-ios-launch.
  --ios-profile-trust-retry-timeout IOS_PROFILE_TRUST_RETRY_TIMEOUT
                        When warm-prime sees ios_profile_not_trusted, keep
                        retrying the missing physical iOS bridge for this many
                        seconds so the operator can trust the developer
                        profile on-device without restarting the matrix
                        command. Defaults to 0, which fails fast.
  --ios-profile-trust-retry-interval IOS_PROFILE_TRUST_RETRY_INTERVAL
                        Seconds between ios_profile_not_trusted warm-prime
                        retry attempts.
  --immediate-role-switch
                        Shortcut for the fastest warm role-switch proof:
                        runtime role switching, role-switch-only, reuse
                        running bridges, require warm bridges, skip build, and
                        skip install. It fails fast instead of falling back to
                        cold launch when a selected bridge is missing.
  --warm-prime-only     Only try to warm selected missing automation bridges,
                        then write warm-bridge-prime.json. This reuses
                        already-running bridges, skips build/install, and does
                        not run role rotations.
  --prime-then-immediate-role-switch
                        Try to warm missing selected bridges first, then run
                        the immediate role-switch proof only if every selected
                        bridge is warm. This skips build/install and writes
                        warm-bridge-prime.json before any rotation artifacts.
  --runtime-role-switch
                        Launch every target once in standby, then rotate
                        master/slave roles through the automation bridge
                        instead of relaunching apps.
  --role-switch-only    Stop after proving the selected master exposes control
                        commands and sees every selected client. No photo or
                        video commands run.
  --repeat-role-switch-cycles REPEAT_ROLE_SWITCH_CYCLES
                        Repeat all selected rotations this many times in one
                        hot runner. Values above 1 require runtime role-switch
                        role-switch-only mode.
  --max-set-role-request-start-skew-ms MAX_SET_ROLE_REQUEST_START_SKEW_MS
                        Fail a runtime role-switch rotation if parallel
                        set_role requests do not begin within this many
                        milliseconds of each other.
  --stage-slaves-after-master-ready
                        In runtime role-switch mode, set the new master first,
                        wait until it exposes master commands, then set all
                        slaves in a parallel batch. This reduces slave
                        connection races against slow master server startup
                        while preserving parallel slave dispatch.
  --fully-parallel-role-switch
                        Diagnostic mode for runtime role-switch proofs: send
                        the promoted master and all slaves in one parallel
                        set_role batch. The immediate shortcuts default to
                        staging the master first because current evidence
                        shows that is faster end-to-end.
  --collect-role-switch-logs
                        Collect per-target logs even for successful role-
                        switch-only rotations. By default logs are collected
                        only on failures.
  --reuse-running-bridges
                        When a target's automation bridge is already healthy
                        and exposes set_role, reuse it instead of terminating
                        and relaunching the app.
  --require-warm-bridges
                        In runtime role-switch reuse mode, fail before
                        build/install/launch unless every selected target
                        already exposes an identity-matched set_role bridge.
[exit-code] 0

